NAME
    mk - execute the current m development materialization capability

SYNOPSIS
    mk materialize <source-root> <definition-root> <useful-root>

DESCRIPTION
    mk is the technical development-lifecycle command. The currently implemented
    public operation is materialize.

    materialize transforms an existing source tree according to an existing
    declarative definition root and publishes the result at a requested useful
    root that does not already exist.

    The current definition requires a scalar type file. The currently supported
    materialization type is copy.

OPERANDS
    <source-root>
        Existing source directory.
    <definition-root>
        Existing declarative materialization definition directory.
    <useful-root>
        Destination pathname whose parent already exists and whose leaf does not.

EXIT STATUS
    0   Success.
    1   Operational, filesystem, definition or materialization failure.
    2   Invalid CLI invocation.
